  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given an array AAA consisting of NNN non-negative integers.\n\nYou need to perform the following operation (N−1)(N - 1)(N−1) times:\n\n\nSort the array AAA in ascending order.\nLet MMM be the current size of the array AAA. Replace the array AAA by [(A2−A1),(A3−A2),…,(AM−AM−1)][(A_2 - A_1), (A_3 - A_2), \\ldots ,(A_M - A_{M-1})][(A2​−A1​),(A3​−A2​),…,(AM​−AM−1​)]. Note that each time the operation is performed, the size of the array reduces by one.\nFind the remaining element after (N−1)(N-1)(N−1) operations.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains an integer TTT denoting number of test cases. The TTT test cases then follow.\nThe first line of each test case contains an integer NNN - the size of the array.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output single line: the remaining element after (N−1)(N-1)(N−1) operations.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "0≤Ai≤10180 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^{18}0≤Ai​≤1018",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n4\n29 19 0 3\n1\n777",
        "output": "1\n777",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 1: The operations look like:\n\nOperation 111: Sort the array. Now, AAA becomes [0,3,19,29][0, 3, 19, 29][0,3,19,29]. Replace the array. Thus, A=[(3−0),(19−3),(29−19)]=[3,16,10]A = [(3-0), (19-3), (29-19)] = [3, 16, 10]A=[(3−0),(19−3),(29−19)]=[3,16,10].\nOperation 222: Sort the array. Now, AAA becomes [3,10,16][3, 10, 16][3,10,16]. Replace the array. Thus, A=[(10−3),(16−10)]=[7,6]A = [(10-3), (16-10)] = [7, 6]A=[(10−3),(16−10)]=[7,6].\nOperation 333: Sort the array. Now, AAA becomes [6,7][6, 7][6,7]. Replace the array. Thus, A=[(7−6)]=[1]A = [(7-6)] = [1]A=[(7−6)]=[1].\n\n\n\nThus, the remaining element after 333 operations is 111.\n\nTest case 2: Since N=1N = 1N=1, you don't need to perform any operation. The remaining element after 000 operations is 777777777."
      }
    ]
  },
